---
title: "Human drawer"
note: "Codie's cabinet body: a precise rectangular seam opens the chest like a drawer that is far deeper than the body, and HOST finds a memory inside. Dial the room, what is found and the ending. The visible pair: a hand that disappears deeper than the torso allows. HOST is your ref image 1; delete (image 1) for text only."
tags: [effects, h3, body_horror, ito]
---
@h3 ref2va 16:9 lite
style: live-action, cinematic surreal body horror, photorealistic
$host = __bh_host__
$room = {a dim study|a wood-panelled library|a quiet bedroom at night}
$memory = {a small faded photograph|a child's red hair ribbon|an old brass house key|a folded handwritten letter}
$ending = {a second, smaller rectangular seam begins forming lower on the abdomen|a tiny keyhole appears just below the collarbone|a faint knock sounds from inside the closed chest}

CAST
HOST (image 1): $host

SHOT 10s | push in, slow
HOST stands facing the camera in $room, framed from the waist up. A thin horizontal seam forms across the upper chest, and two short vertical seams descend from its ends into a precise rectangle; a small dark handle-like ridge rises at its centre. HOST grips the ridge and slides the rectangular section of the chest outward as one intact volume, like precision cabinetry that keeps its human surface. It keeps coming, far deeper than the body could hold, until the chest drawer extends nearly an arm's length; inside is a dark smooth cavity. HOST reaches in, and the arm disappears past the body's visible depth, the forearm, then part of the upper arm. HOST searches with quiet curiosity and draws out $memory, looks at it briefly, returns it and pushes the drawer back until the seams are almost invisible. HOST places a palm on the closed chest and looks at the camera. In the final moment $ending.
SFX: quiet room ambience; restrained breathing; a smooth wooden sliding sound; a hollow resonance from the deep interior; a soft click as the chest closes
MUSIC: N/A
